Z||000010||fropuff||09-06-2000||09:31 PM||||Thanks.  I guess I don't have to download them on the board now.  My dad's doing the rest at work tomorrow.  There are quite a few.  I think they turned out nice.  No, I did not do the job myself.  I did, however, do all the bodywork and sanding.  That really sucks!  I spent about 90% of my summer sanding.  That's what I did the whole 3 months.  I think it was worth it, though.  The preparation is the key.  The painting didn't turn out the best, but I don't really care!  There is only one spot that turned out not so good.  It was where the painter guy filled in a deep chip on the front hood with Bondo (near the right side headlamp cover) and didn't sand it the best.  That's the only think he sanded, and it didn't turn out good at all.  You can see the raise in it and the outline of it.  If I get some hood scoops like fieroshop's, I will probably get the entire thing repainted professionally.  Then it will look 99% good.  There are a few other minor glitches; oh well.  Thanks for posting them on here, BroCar.  I'm sorry to those that I sent them to;  I finally figured out that the pictures on both e-mails were the exact same!  I downloaded it 3 times to figure it out.  Sorry.  There should be some more coming tomorrow to those who want to see them, and if BroCar wouldn't mind posting them.....That would be great.  Thanks again.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fropuff||09-12-2000||05:09 PM||||I got some more pictures scanned.  Although I have them, my stupid, piece-of-crap computer can't download the Pennock's image poster.  I don't want to e-mail them to anybody, as they take 32 minutes a piece to download.  They are a .bmp file, so that's why it takes so long.  .jpg files are a lot better.  What should I do?  Thanks.||||reg||1
